From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:46:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Cut allocations in damage, font-face and inline-root
 bookkeeping

Layout bookkeeping allocated on every pass:

- The damage summary folds in one pass over the nodes instead of collecting a list that
  doubled as it grew (6.3 MB of copies on html.spec.whatwg.org).
- The font-face scan lowercases each family atom once, not per lookup (1.1M allocations).
  Text spans borrow their family names, and the pending-face check allocates nothing.
- Each inline root enters the inline-root index once while it holds its layout, tracked by
  a bit on its TextLayout, rather than on every box construction. The index shrinks after
  pruning when under half full; it held 262,144 slots for 56.7k roots.
- The text-node range buffer is reused across inline layout builds.

On html.spec.whatwg.org, allocations fall from 6.64M to 4.52M and realloc copies from
75.9 to 45.8 MB, together with the attribute-collection and id-map patches that follow
and the matching parley, parley_engine and taffy changes.
Output is unchanged.
